              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 375,
                "end_index": 503,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Consistency and Texture (The Biggest Difference)\n* **Dosa Masala:** This is a **dry or semi-dry, thick, and chunky** potato mash"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                2,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 505,
                "end_index": 591,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because it is spread directly inside a hot, crispy dosa, it must have minimal moisture"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 593,
                "end_index": 665,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "If it is too wet, the steam and water will instantly make the dosa soggy"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 667,
                "end_index": 747,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Poori Masala:** This has a **flowy, gravy-like, or semi-liquid** consistency"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 749,
                "end_index": 896,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Since pooris are puffed, hollow, deep-fried breads, you need a saucy consistency so you can easily tear off a piece of poori and scoop up the curry"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 906,
                "end_index": 1018,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The Use of Besan (Gram Flour)\n* **Dosa Masala:** Gram flour (besan) is **never used** in traditional dosa masala"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1020,
                "end_index": 1079,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The potatoes are simply mashed to hold the mixture together"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                4,
                6
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1081,
                "end_index": 1246,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Poori Masala:** In most \"hotel-style\" South Indian recipes, a small amount of **besan slurry** (gram flour mixed with water) is stirred into the boiling potatoes"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                6,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1248,
                "end_index": 1383,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This acts as a thickener, giving the gravy a silky, glossy, cohesive texture and preventing the water from separating from the potatoes"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                7
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1406,
                "end_index": 1489,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Lemon Juice (The Sour Agent)\n* **Dosa Masala:** Typically, **no tomatoes** are used"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                9,
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1491,
                "end_index": 1692,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Since dosa batter is already naturally fermented and slightly sour, the potato filling is kept mild, with a simple squeeze of fresh **lemon or lime juice** added at the very end for a clean, sharp tang"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1694,
                "end_index": 1789,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Poori Masala:** Frequently includes **finely chopped tomatoes** cooked down with the onions"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1791,
                "end_index": 1917,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "The tomatoes add moisture, build the gravy base, and provide a sweet, cooked tanginess that pairs beautifully with fried dough"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 1927,
                "end_index": 2109,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Textural Role of the Tempering (Dals)\n* **Dosa Masala:** The tempering (tadka) of mustard seeds, chana dal (split chickpeas), and urad dal (split black gram) is saut\u00e9ed until golden"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                10
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2111,
                "end_index": 2185,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Because the dish is dry, these lentils retain a **distinct, crunchy bite**"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2187,
                "end_index": 2264,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "This provides a wonderful texture alongside the soft potatoes and crispy dosa"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                5
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2266,
                "end_index": 2373,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Poori Masala:** While the same lentils are used for tempering, they simmer in the added water and gravy"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                8,
                3
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2451,
                "end_index": 2603,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "Additional Vegetables\n* **Dosa Masala:** Strictly focuses on potatoes and plenty of sliced onions, seasoned with green chilies, ginger, and curry leaves"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                11,
                12
              ],
              "segment": {
                "start_index": 2606,
                "end_index": 2776,
                "part_index": null,
                "text": "* **Poori Masala:** Is more forgiving and often includes other vegetables like **green peas (matar) or carrots** to add color, sweetness, and variety to the dipping gravy"
              },
              "rendered_parts": null
            },
            {
              "confidence_scores": null,
              "grounding_chunk_indices": [
                0,
